  "title": "Control board floorplan B - DSP rotated 90 deg, PWM/fault/ADC-A side facing the mezzanine header (review-corrected)",
  "status": "AI-GENERATED ENGINEERING PROTOTYPE - V2 - HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED",
  "description": "TMS320F28335 (U5) rotated 90 deg so that pins 1-44 (GPIO0-17 PWM/fault lines and ADCINA0-A7) face the 2 x 25 mezzanine header J8 along the bottom edge; the former bottom side (ADCINB, GPIO18-27, JTAG) faces the right-hand analogue section, XCLKIN faces the oscillator above the DSP and the boot/UART pins face the left strip. Review corrections (verification/layout_review_findings.json): J8 on B.Cu so the header mates downward into the power-board socket (LR-03); the DSP moved 2 mm up and the fault/PWM logic region moved below y = 57 mm so the 43 south-side escapes have a 10 mm routing band (LR-02); the eight 1 nF ADC filters and the ADCREF capacitors in a dedicated strip beside the ADC pins (LR-04); the 5 V buck input ceramics C4/C5 at the TPS54302 pins, 5V_SW/5V_BST as pre-routed F.Cu tracks with C6 at the pins (LR-05); 2 x 4 via arrays in the two exposed pads (LR-06); 12V_IN as a 1.0 mm F.Cu bus and a three-via group at the eFuse output (LR-07); J4/J5 at the left edge next to J2 (LR-09); 3V3 bypass ring at 18.0 mm (LR-13); Y1 beside XCLKIN (LR-16). Supplies (eFuse, 5 V buck, dual LDO) in the top-left corner, 12V_PROT running down the left column to mezzanine pins 1-3, LDO 1V9 output in a corridor island feeding the DSP core island on In2.Cu, JTAG at the top-right edge (F.Cu, accessible with the board stacked), status LEDs and E-stop at the right edge, NTC at the lower right.",
